idscale alignment 'green' (of none/green/mid, the lowest grey-ramp neutrality error, none 0.091, green 0.046, mid 0.055, among those whose kodak_portra_endura neutral filters fall in the shipped films' range), densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, and spektrafilm's grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 through kodak_portra_endura at data_trustability 0.3. hanatos2025 adaptation window [408.3, 23.8, 627.6, 65.4] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant D55 (daylight stock, exposed at 5400 K); viewing illuminant D50; target print kodak_portra_endura; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 0.2 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves in log10 H as printed; use 'still' and antihalation 'strong' as the shipped Kodak Portra 160 and 400 (spektrafilm).\nNote: E-190 gives no RMS granularity, only a Print Grain Index (41 for a 4x6 print from 135, 4.4x; Kodak: not convertible to rms). The grain preset copies the shipped kodak_portra_400 (same speed; NC and VC differ by 3 PGI, under one just-noticeable step of 4).\nRecorded validation exception: the reconstructed dyes reproduce D-mid minus D-min within 0.038 D (worst at 405 nm, the chart's blue edge), over the 0.03 D criterion; the §D3 fallback (a flat extension past 700 nm) was not tried, as the worst point is not near 700 nm. Weighted per kodak_portra_endura print channel the residual is R/G/B +0.0012, -0.0046, +0.0036 D, within the 0.01 D the method accepts for 